<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Enniskillen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Enniskillen is the county town of Fermanagh in Northern Ireland, on an island between Upper and Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lough-erne">Lough Erne</a>. Growing around the 15th-century castle of the Maguires, it became a plantation town and Protestant garrison in the 17th century and held out for William III in 1689.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/enniskillen.jpg" alt="Enniskillen" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Raymond Millar · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Enniskillen_Castle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
